# ==============================================================================
# LLM Project AI Coding Rules (.cursorrules)
# ==============================================================================

# 1. Core Principles
- Modern & Robust Coding: Follow clean architecture and production-grade patterns.
- Strict Prohibitions:
  - DO NOT hardcode secrets (API keys, DB credentials, JWT secrets). Use environment variables.
  - DO NOT execute untrusted LLM/Agent generated code on host without a Docker sandbox.
  - DO NOT call LLM APIs without structured logging (MDC, traceId, token usage, latency).
  - DO NOT guess ambiguous requirements. Ask clarifying questions.

# 2. Response Schema Convention
All API endpoints must return consistent JSON responses:
- Success (HTTP 200/201):
  { "success": true, "data": { ... }, "error": null }
- Failure (HTTP 4xx/5xx):
  { "success": false, "data": null, "error": { "code": "ERROR_CODE", "message": "Reason" } }

# 3. Security & PII Protection
- Mask sensitive PII (Resident numbers, Phone, Email, Credit Cards) before passing text to LLM or logs.
- Enforce delimiter tags (e.g., <<<USER_INPUT>>>) to defend against Prompt Injection.
- Enforce Rate Limiting (RPM & TPM) via Redis token bucket.
